ider outright short positions if comfortable with timing and risk management. - Tighten stop-loss orders to protect against potential downside surprises. - Maintain liquidity to capitalize on better entry points if the stock declines further. - Stay vigilant about macroeconomic indicators and upcoming product launches, but with a conservative bias.  In summary, given the headwinds and current valuation signals, I recommend a short-term Sell position. This allows us to protect capital while remaining attentive to any new developments that might alter the risk landscape.
